messages:
Ava M.: Quick sync — we need a final narrative + visuals for the benchmark launch next week. Focus: show how serving choices change real dollars and SLA outcomes. Two asks: 1) a concise hero claim for the launch post; 2) one standalone chart and one composite that will work on social + blog.
Samir P.: Love it. For hero claim: two directions — (A) "Predictable latency, predictable spend" and (B) "Same model. Smarter serving. Lower bills." Which do you want to test first? :thinking_face:
Ava M.: Both. We'll A/B headline on the blog landing and use the stronger on socials. Samir — can you draft short variants (20–30 chars) for social, and a slightly longer subhead for the blog? 
Samir P.: On it. Drafts by EOD. A: "Predictable latency, predictable spend" (social: "Predictable latency. Predictable cost.") B: "Same model. Smarter serving. Lower bills." (social: "Smarter serving = lower bills")
Jen O.: Data to highlight in charts: p50 single-request latency = 120ms, p95 = 420ms for our hosted profile; tokens/sec throughput for dedicated config = ~4k tokens/s; observed token cost delta between naive serving and our recommended profile = 2.5x reduction. Also average customer request length = 68 tokens. 
Elena G.: For visuals: propose a three-panel horizontal asset: left panel — 'latency distribution' violin with p50/p95 markers; middle — 'cost per 1k tokens' bar comparing naive vs optimized vs quantized; right — 'routing map' small flow diagram showing fastpath vs slowpath and fallback. Keep colors aligned with redwood palette (deep blue, teal, warm gray).
Noah B.: For conversion, we should wire inbound tags: "bench-interest" and "high-touch". If lead has company_size > 200 or estimated monthly tokens > 200M -> route to Sales SDR queue. Otherwise go to Growth. Can we get a sample rule for the engineers? 
Ravi C.: Sample rule (copy for routing-bot):
```
if (lead.tags.includes('bench-interest')) {
  if (lead.company_size > 200 || lead.estimated_monthly_tokens > 200000000) {
    tag('high-touch'); assign('sales-sdr');
  } else {
    assign('growth-nurture');
  }
}
```
Elena G.: For the blog composite image, also include a tiny annotation under the cost chart: "Costs shown are inference-only, normalized per 1k tokens; infra & data costs vary." Keep that as thin copy so legal is happy.
Jen O.: One more data nugget we should call out in copy: median cost per request for typical prompt size (68 tokens) drops from ~$0.0042 -> ~$0.0017 with our recommended pipeline. That's a 2.47x saving — nice headline stat.
Ava M.: Perfect. Samir, please bake that number into the "developer-first" and "cost-first" variants. Also give me CTA options: "Try the benchmark runner", "See our cost calculator", "Request a latency demo".
Samir P.: Will do. I'll push two headline variants + 3 social captions + 3 CTAs by EOD. 
Noah B.: Webinar idea: 20-min product demo + 25-min Q&A with a small customer case study. Landing form includes a mandatory 'estimated monthly tokens' field so routing rules get clean signals. :white_check_mark:
Ava M.: Love the webinar plan. Jen — can you surface the token-distribution heatmap by tomorrow so we can show sample traffic slices in the slides? 
Jen O.: Yep — exporting now. Will drop a PNG in the design channel and ping you. 
routing-bot: Rule created in staging: bench-interest -> growth-nurture / sales-sdr per conditions. Use /deploy-route to push to prod.
Ava M.: Great progress. After Samir's copy, Elena can mock the three-panel image. We'll review tomorrow 10:30am. :thumbsup:
